Package: ROpenManim
Type: Package
Title: Mathematical Animation Engine for R
Version: 0.0.4
Authors@R: person("Qing", "Zhu", email = "20170458@alu.cqu.edu.cn",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A scene-graph and animation engine in the spirit of Manim, but
    implemented natively in R.  A frame is compiled into a list of drawing
    instructions (path / stroke / image) and handed to a pluggable backend;
    the default backend draws with 'grid' onto any R graphics device, so a
    video is just a sequence of device frames encoded by 'av'.  Text is
    converted to real outlines through 'systemfonts', and LaTeX formulas are
    compiled with 'dvisvgm' into Bezier paths, which means formulas and text
    are ordinary vector objects that can be transformed, faded and morphed
    rather than pasted as bitmaps.  Camera geometry follows Manim: a frame is
    8 units tall with a 16:9 aspect ratio.
License: GPL-2
Encoding: UTF-8
URL: https://github.com/Judy-ZQ/ROpenManim
BugReports: https://github.com/Judy-ZQ/ROpenManim/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: R6, grDevices, grid, systemfonts, av, utils, stats, tools
Suggests: knitr, tinytex
SystemRequirements: Only needed for optional features: a LaTeX installation
    providing dvisvgm is required by mathtex(). Video encoding is handled by
    the 'av' package, whose Windows binary bundles FFmpeg, so no separate
    ffmpeg install and no Rtools are needed.
NeedsCompilation: no
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
